\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Supervised fine-tuning loss}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{supervised-fine-tuning}
\tag{loss}

\p{Let #{D_{\mathrm{sft}}} be a finite multiset of instruction-tuning
records. For #{y=(y_1,\ldots,y_{|y|})}, the \strong{supervised fine-tuning
loss} with response-token normalization is}

##{
 L_{\mathrm{sft}}(\theta)
 =-\frac{1}{N_D}
   \sum_{(x,y)\in D_{\mathrm{sft}}}
   \sum_{t=1}^{|y|}
   \log \pi_\theta(y_t\mid x,y_{<t}),
 \qquad
 N_D=\sum_{(x,y)\in D_{\mathrm{sft}}}|y|.
}

\p{Section 3.5 and Appendix C.1 of \citef{ouyang2022training} describe the
supervised stage and its training settings. The displayed response-token
normalization is an FTIP convention; the source does not disclose this exact
normalization. Prompt-token masking and record-level normalization are other
conventions and must be stated when used.}
